{"id":"mahabharata-3-290","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":290,"title":"नवत्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 290 · Kunti summons the Sun","summary":{"en":"Out of girlish curiosity Kunti tries the mantra on the rising Sun, and the god appears before her. When she begs him to go back, he refuses, saying he cannot return in vain, and insists that she give herself to him and bear a son like himself.","kn":"ಬಾಲಕುತೂಹಲದಿಂದ ಕುಂತಿ ಉದಯಿಸುತ್ತಿರುವ ಸೂರ್ಯನ ಮೇಲೆ ಮಂತ್ರ ಪ್ರಯೋಗಿಸುತ್ತಾಳೆ, ದೇವನು ಅವಳೆದುರು ಪ್ರತ್ಯಕ್ಷನಾಗುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಹಿಂದಿರುಗೆಂದು ಬೇಡಿದಾಗ ವ್ಯರ್ಥವಾಗಿ ಮರಳಲಾರೆನೆಂದು ನಿರಾಕರಿಸಿ ತನ್ನನ್ನು ಸೇರಿ ತನ್ನಂಥ ಮಗನನ್ನು ಪಡೆ ಎಂದು ಒತ್ತಾಯಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"बालसुलभ कौतूहल से कुन्ती उगते सूर्य पर मन्त्र आज़माती हैं, और देवता उनके सामने प्रकट हो जाते हैं। जब वे उनसे लौट जाने की विनती करती हैं, वे मना करते हैं कि व्यर्थ नहीं लौट सकते, और आग्रह करते हैं कि वे उनसे मिलें और उन जैसा पुत्र पाएँ।","te":"బాల్య కుతూహలంతో కుంతి ఉదయిస్తున్న సూర్యునిపై మంత్రం ప్రయోగిస్తుంది, దేవుడు ఆమె ఎదుట ప్రత్యక్షమవుతాడు. తిరిగి వెళ్లమని వేడుకోగా వృథాగా తిరిగివెళ్లలేనని నిరాకరించి తనతో కలిసి తనవంటి కుమారుని పొందమని పట్టుబడతాడు.","ta":"சிறுமிக்குரிய ஆர்வத்தால் குந்தி உதயமாகும் சூரியனிடம் மந்திரத்தை முயல, தேவன் அவள் முன் தோன்றுகிறான். திரும்பிச் செல்லுமாறு அவள் வேண்ட, வீணாகத் திரும்ப முடியாது என்று மறுத்துத் தன்னுடன் கூடித் தன்னைப் போன்ற மகனைப் பெறுமாறு வலியுறுத்துகிறான்.","ml":"ബാലികയുടെ കൗതുകത്താൽ കുന്തി ഉദിക്കുന്ന സൂര്യനിൽ മന്ത്രം പരീക്ഷിക്കുന്നു; ദേവൻ അവളുടെ മുന്നിൽ പ്രത്യക്ഷപ്പെടുന്നു. അവൾ മടങ്ങിപ്പോകാൻ അപേക്ഷിക്കുമ്പോൾ, വെറുംകൈയോടെ മടങ്ങാനാവില്ലെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു; തന്നോടൊപ്പം ചേർന്ന് തനിക്ക് തുല്യനായ ഒരു പുത്രനെ പ്രസവിക്കണമെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം നിർബന്ധിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.290; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"कुण्डलाहरणपर्व","titleEn":"Kundalaharana Parva (Taking of the earrings)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"गते तस्मिन्द्विजश्रेष्ठे कस्मिंश्चित्कालपर्यये ।\nचिन्तयामास सा कन्या मन्त्रग्रामबलाबलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"After that best of brahmins had gone, after some time, the girl thought about the power and weakness of the mantras."}},{"n":2,"text":"अयं वै कीदृशस्तेन मम दत्तो महात्मना ।\nमन्त्रग्रामो बलं तस्य ज्ञास्ये नातिचिरादिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"What kind of thing is this mantra-set that the great one gave me? I shall soon learn its power."}},{"n":3,"text":"एवं संचिन्तयन्ती सा ददर्शर्तुं यदृच्छया ।\nव्रीडिता साभवद्बाला कन्याभावे रजस्वला ॥","meaning":{"en":"As she thought this, she happened to see her own menstrual period, and the girl was ashamed, while still unmarried."}},{"n":4,"text":"अथोद्यन्तं सहस्रांशुं पृथा दीप्तं ददर्श ह ।\nन ततर्प च रूपेण भानोः संध्यागतस्य सा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Pritha saw the thousand-rayed sun rising, blazing; she could not take her fill of the sight of the sun at dawn."}},{"n":5,"text":"तस्या दृष्टिरभूद्दिव्या सापश्यद्दिव्यदर्शनम् ।\nआमुक्तकवचं देवं कुण्डलाभ्यां विभूषितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Her sight became divine, and she saw the god of divine appearance, wearing armor and adorned with earrings."}},{"n":6,"text":"तस्याः कौतूहलं त्वासीन्मन्त्रं प्रति नराधिप ।\nआह्वानमकरोत्साथ तस्य देवस्य भामिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Curiosity about the mantra arose in her, king, and the lady made the call to that god."}},{"n":7,"text":"प्राणानुपस्पृश्य तदा आजुहाव दिवाकरम् ।\nआजगाम ततो राजंस्त्वरमाणो दिवाकरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Touching water, she called the day-maker; and then, king, Surya came in haste."}},{"n":8,"text":"मधुपिङ्गो महाबाहुः कम्बुग्रीवो हसन्निव ।\nअङ्गदी बद्धमुकुटो दिशः प्रज्वालयन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Honey-tawny, mighty-armed, conch-necked, as if smiling, wearing armlets and a crown, he lit up the quarters as though ablaze."}},{"n":9,"text":"योगात्कृत्वा द्विधात्मानमाजगाम तताप च ।\nआबभाषे ततः कुन्तीं साम्ना परमवल्गुना ॥","meaning":{"en":"By yoga, making himself two, he came and also shone in the sky; then he spoke to Kunti with very gentle and soothing words."}},{"n":10,"text":"आगतोऽस्मि वशं भद्रे तव मन्त्रबलात्कृतः ।\nकिं करोम्यवशो राज्ञि ब्रूहि कर्ता तदस्मि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have come under your power, good lady, drawn by the force of your mantra. What shall I do, queen, helpless as I am? Say, and I will do it."}},{"text":"कुन्त्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Kunti said:"}},{"n":11,"text":"गम्यतां भगवंस्तत्र यतोऽसि समुपागतः ।\nकौतूहलात्समाहूतः प्रसीद भगवन्निति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Go back, lord, to where you came from; I called you out of curiosity. Be gracious, lord."}},{"text":"सूर्य उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Surya said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"गमिष्येऽहं यथा मां त्वं ब्रवीषि तनुमध्यमे ।\nन तु देवं समाहूय न्याय्यं प्रेषयितुं वृथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"I shall go as you tell me, slender-waisted one, but it is not right to send away a god once called, for nothing."}},{"n":13,"text":"तवाभिसंधिः सुभगे सूर्यात्पुत्रो भवेदिति ।\nवीर्येणाप्रतिमो लोके कवची कुण्डलीति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fortunate one, your intention was to have a son from the sun, unequaled in the world in valor, with armor and earrings."}},{"n":14,"text":"सा त्वमात्मप्रदानं वै कुरुष्व गजगामिनि ।\nउत्पत्स्यति हि पुत्रस्ते यथासंकल्पमङ्गने ॥","meaning":{"en":"So give yourself to me, elephant-gaited one; a son will be born to you as you intended, lady."}},{"n":15,"text":"अथ गच्छाम्यहं भद्रे त्वयासंगम्य सुस्मिते ।\nशप्स्यामि त्वामहं क्रुद्धो ब्राह्मणं पितरं च ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"If I go without uniting with you, good lady with the sweet smile, I shall be angry and curse you, the brahmin, and your father."}},{"n":16,"text":"त्वत्कृते तान्प्रधक्ष्यामि सर्वानपि न संशयः ।\nपितरं चैव ते मूढं यो न वेत्ति तवानयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For your sake I will burn all of them, without doubt, and your foolish father who does not know of your misdeed."}},{"n":17,"text":"तस्य च ब्राह्मणस्याद्य योऽसौ मन्त्रमदात्तव ।\nशीलवृत्तमविज्ञाय धास्यामि विनयं परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And that brahmin who gave you the mantra without knowing your character, I shall teach a great lesson today."}},{"n":18,"text":"एते हि विबुधाः सर्वे पुरंदरमुखा दिवि ।\nत्वया प्रलब्धं पश्यन्ति स्मयन्त इव भामिनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"All these gods in heaven, led by Indra, see you cheated, lady, as if smiling."}},{"n":19,"text":"पश्य चैनान्सुरगणान्दिव्यं चक्षुरिदं हि ते ।\nपूर्वमेव मया दत्तं दृष्टवत्यसि येन माम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Look at these hosts of gods; this divine sight was given to you earlier by me, with which you have seen me."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":20,"text":"ततोऽपश्यत्त्रिदशान्राजपुत्री\nसर्वानेव स्वेषु धिष्ण्येषु खस्थान् ।\nप्रभासन्तं भानुमन्तं महान्तं\nयथादित्यं रोचमानं तथैव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the princess saw all the gods standing in the sky in their own abodes, and the great Sun, shining like the radiant one himself."}},{"n":21,"text":"सा तान्दृष्ट्वा व्रीडमानेव बाला\nसूर्यं देवी वचनं प्राह भीता ।\nगच्छ त्वं वै गोपते स्वं विमानं\nकन्याभावाद्दुःख एषोपचारः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing them, the girl, ashamed and frightened, said to the sun god: Lord of rays, go to your own heavenly car; it is painful to submit while I am unmarried."}},{"n":22,"text":"पिता माता गुरवश्चैव येऽन्ये\nदेहस्यास्य प्रभवन्ति प्रदाने ।\nनाहं धर्मं लोपयिष्यामि लोके\nस्त्रीणां वृत्तं पूज्यते देहरक्षा ॥","meaning":{"en":"My father, mother and elders, and others, have authority over giving this body. I will not violate dharma in the world; for women, protecting the body is the honored way."}},{"n":23,"text":"मया मन्त्रबलं ज्ञातुमाहूतस्त्वं विभावसो ।\nबाल्याद्बालेति कृत्वा तत्क्षन्तुमर्हसि मे विभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"I called you, maker of light, only to test the power of the mantra; since I am a child, forgive me, lord."}},{"text":"सूर्य उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Surya said:"}},{"n":24,"text":"बालेति कृत्वानुनयं तवाहं\nददानि नान्यानुनयं लभेत ।\nआत्मप्रदानं कुरु कुन्तिकन्ये\nशान्तिस्तवैवं हि भवेच्च भीरु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because you are a child, I will give you leave, but no one else would get it. Give yourself, daughter of Kunti; thus will there be peace for you, timid one."}},{"n":25,"text":"न चापि युक्तं गन्तुं हि मया मिथ्याकृतेन वै ।\nगमिष्याम्यनवद्याङ्गि लोके समवहास्यताम् ।\nसर्वेषां विबुधानां च वक्तव्यः स्यामहं शुभे ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is not right for me to go back having been made false; I would be laughed at in the world, blameless one, and spoken of by all the gods."}},{"n":26,"text":"सा त्वं मया समागच्छ पुत्रं लप्स्यसि मादृशम् ।\nविशिष्टा सर्वलोकेषु भविष्यसि च भामिनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"So come together with me, and you will have a son like me, and you will be distinguished among all worlds, good lady."}}]}]}